      "description": "Watch Huracan vs Banfield highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 25, 2026. On July 25, 2026 , the Liga Profesional Argentina played host to a gritty encounter between Huracán and Banfield . Both sides stepped onto the pitch with a clear defensive resolve, setting the stage for a tactical battle where patience would be the ultimate virtue. A Cautious Opening Exchange The match began with high physical stakes but limited goalmouth action. Banfield faced an early tactical hurdle when Facundo Waller was forced off in the 30th minute, replaced by Facundo Kalinger . The tension in the midfield was palpable, leading to the game's first booking when David Zalazar received a yellow card in the 36th minute for a late challenge. As the first half progressed, both defenses remained organized, successfully neutralizing any attacking threats. The flow of the game was frequently interrupted by fouls, preventing either side from establishing a dominant rhythm. By the time the referee blew for halftime, the deadlock remained unbroken, leaving everything to play for in the second period. Caicedo Breaks the Deadlock The second half saw an increase in urgency. Following a yellow card for Santiago Esquivel in the 56th minute, the momentum began to shift. The breakthrough finally arrived in the 65th minute when Leonardo Gil provided a brilliant assist for Jordy Caicedo . The striker made no mistake, firing the ball home to give Huracán the lead and fundamentally changing the complexion of the match. In the closing stages, Banfield pushed forward in search of an equalizer, introducing several substitutes including Federico Anselmo and Neyder no . However, Huracán stood firm, managing the game with experience. Despite late yellow cards for Cesar Ibanez and Tomas Adoryan , and a tense six minutes of stoppage time, the home side held on to secure a hard-fought victory."
